+## Failed session initialization
+
+- If `beforeSession` rejects with an `Error`, the orchestrator awaits `onError(session, error)` and then `afterSession(session)` before rejecting to the caller with that same error, provided those hooks complete normally; no user-input or model-response work runs for that turn ([validated by: reports and cleans up a failed beforeSession before rejecting with the original error](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
+
+`afterSession` is an unconditional cleanup hook, including when initialization fails partway through. It receives the same session, with no new started flag; it cannot assume that initialization finished or that any model work happened. Deployers must track which resources their `beforeSession` acquired and release only those resources in `afterSession`. This is the intended contract for #94, replacing the previously recorded skipped-cleanup flaw.
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
